A||||4||speed racer||where to look for rust||||1||
Z||000000||speed racer||10-28-2001||09:14 PM||||Where is the key places to look for rust on a Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Master_Sushi||10-28-2001||09:31 PM||||Good Question  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">...<P>I have an 84SE I bought a few months ago and have been restoring. This fiero had insane rust on it. I had to replace *allot* of sheet metal with my welder to make it driveable. Correct me if I am wrong but this is how fieros seem to rust out to me.<P>1st- Battery tray gets rusty and/or falls apart. Surface rust gets a bit above normal on frame.<P>2nd- In the trunk area around the sides, they get big nasty cancer holes in them.<P>3rd- The floor board start to go out, this is a PITA to fix. <P>4th- This seems the worst, the strut towers in the back start to rust. They will get so bad they will just fall apart around the welds and pop up! This is not good and very dangerous!!! <P>All of these happend to my fiero but a little creative welding fixed everything. Watch out for rust on fieros. They hide it very well.||||reg||2
Z||000002||roadwarrior||10-28-2001||09:38 PM||||the worst place I found on my 84 se is the upper rear frame rails and the engine craddle I've had my car since july and I'm still finding new rust not to mention fixing spots that I have already found, hope ya know how to weld laddy. but I don't agree that they hide the rust extremely well on fiero's, there's just so much of it that we don't know where to start looking. Lol||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroBUZZ||10-28-2001||09:55 PM||||As Master_S says.  Also, underside where the cooling tubes run (under rocker panels).  Look under the front end at mounting points and bracketry for the front fascia and the front bumper crash panel. Look in the holes where the front turn signals are.  Light buckets, door frames, rocker panels under the plastic, around the windshield under the roof panel.<BR>That's a start.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000004||Master_Sushi||10-28-2001||10:31 PM||||DO I know how to weld?!?!?!<P>um... not really  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I basicly learned how to on the car..... I just need to drive back and forth from work/classes to use it as my winter car. If it lasts tell the spring I will be happy! I dont know if Ill bother to sell it or not, its so riged up that im the only one who knows how to really drive it. Its an ultimate expression of my personality  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!<P>lol, funny thing is this is how most fieros I see are now...||||reg||1
